# The artifact-bake surface: infra/deploy/Dockerfile.artifacts and nothing else.
#
# Its own lock, deliberately. `wandb` is the ONE dependency in this repository whose install
# would otherwise happen unhashed, and it is the dependency of the one image that ever holds
# a credential -- fetching the registry client without hash verification, inside the build
# that mounts WANDB_API_KEY, is the exact circularity premortem C11 is about, pointed at the
# worst possible target.
#
# It is NOT folded into requirements/dev.lock: nothing in the test suite imports wandb (the
# tracking module's calls are injected through `artifact_factory`), and the closure below
# drags in gitpython, protobuf, sentry-sdk and psutil, none of which belong in the
# environment the unit job installs.
#
# It is also NOT installed by any serving image. The serving path fetches the artifact at
# deploy time through infra/deploy/instance/fetch_artifacts.sh, under the instance profile,
# with no registry client on the box at all.
wandb==0.18.5
